 "title": "Dizziness: first decide whether it is true vertigo; non-vestibular dizziness has organic and psychiatric causes, while peripheral vertigo is named by how long attacks last and whether hearing is affected: BPPV, Meniere's disease, vestibular neuronitis or labyrinthitis, superior canal dehiscence, and aminoglycoside toxicity; each column gives presentation, investigations and treatment",
